{"name":"Cotton Flannel","hex":"#9090a2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cotton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous substance:\n A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium.\n Any similar soft, fibrous, white substance of fine hairs, of any origin.","A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of cotton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotton"},{"term":"flannel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft cloth material originally woven from wool, today often combined with cotton or synthetic fibers.","A washcloth."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of flannel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flannel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flannel","blocks":[{"text":"Flannel is a soft woven fabric of varying fineness. Flannel was originally made from carded wool or worsted yarn, but is now often made from either wool, cotton, or synthetic fiber. Flannel is commonly used to make tartan clothing, blankets, bed sheets, sleepwear, and several other uses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Flannel_Shirt_For_Abi.jpg/330px-Flannel_Shirt_For_Abi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flannel"},{"title":"Cotton","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton is a soft, fluffy staple fiber that grows in a boll, or protective case, around the seeds of the cotton plants of the genus Gossypium in the mallow family Malvaceae. The fiber is almost pure cellulose and may contain minor percentages of waxes, fats, pectins, and water. Under natural conditions, cotton bolls facilitate the dispersal of the seeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CottonPla